## Article 349. Powers of cassation court

```catala
declaration scope Article349CassationPowers:
  input check content CassationPowersCheck
  output mayLeaveUnsatisfied content YesNo
  output mayCancelAndSendForNewReview content YesNo
  output mayCancelAndNewDecision content YesNo
  output mayCancelAppealKeepFirstInstance content YesNo
  output mayCancelAndCloseOrLeave content YesNo
  output mayInvalidateAndClose content YesNo

scope Article349CassationPowers:
# Leave unsatisfied when decisions correct
  label leave_unsatisfied definition mayLeaveUnsatisfied under condition
    check.decisionsCorrect = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_leave definition mayLeaveUnsatisfied equals No

# Cancel and send for new review when cancellation ground exists
  label cancel_new_review definition mayCancelAndSendForNewReview under condition
    check.cancellationGroundExists = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_cancel_new_review definition mayCancelAndSendForNewReview equals No

# Cancel and adopt new decision
  label cancel_new definition mayCancelAndNewDecision under condition
    check.cancellationGroundExists = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_cancel_new definition mayCancelAndNewDecision equals No

# Cancel appeal court decision, keep first instance
  label cancel_appeal definition mayCancelAppealKeepFirstInstance under condition
    check.appealCourtCancelledCorrectFirstInstance = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_cancel_appeal definition mayCancelAppealKeepFirstInstance equals No

# Cancel and close or leave without consideration
  label cancel_close definition mayCancelAndCloseOrLeave under condition
    check.closureOrLeaveWithoutConsiderationGround = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_cancel_close definition mayCancelAndCloseOrLeave equals No

# Invalidate and close
  label invalidate definition mayInvalidateAndClose under condition
    check.jurisdictionViolation = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_invalidate definition mayInvalidateAndClose equals No
```

## Article 350. Grounds for leaving cassation complaint unsatisfied

```catala
declaration scope Article350CassationLeaveUnsatisfied:
  input check content CassationLeaveUnsatisfiedCheck
  output decisionsCorrect content YesNo

scope Article350CassationLeaveUnsatisfied:
# Decisions correct when properly applied law
  label correct definition decisionsCorrect under condition
    check.firstInstanceCorrect = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

# Not overturned for procedural violations that did not affect outcome
  label procedural_excused definition decisionsCorrect under condition
    check.proceduralViolationDidNotAffectOutcome = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label incorrect definition decisionsCorrect equals No
```

## Article 351. Grounds for cancellation and new decision

```catala
declaration scope Article351CassationCancellationNewDecision:
  input check content CassationCancellationNewDecisionCheck
  output cancellationForNewDecision content YesNo

scope Article351CassationCancellationNewDecision:
# Cancel when wrong substantive law applied
  label wrong_law definition cancellationForNewDecision under condition
    check.wrongSubstantiveLaw = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

# Cancel when procedural violation affected outcome
  label procedural definition cancellationForNewDecision under condition
    check.proceduralViolationAffectedOutcome = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_cancellation definition cancellationForNewDecision equals No
```

## Article 352. Grounds for cancelling appeal court decision and keeping first instance

```catala
declaration scope Article352CancelAppealKeepFirstInstance:
  input check content CassationCancelAppealCheck
  output appealMustBeCancelled content YesNo

scope Article352CancelAppealKeepFirstInstance:
# Cancel appeal decision when first instance was correct
  label cancel definition appealMustBeCancelled under condition
    check.appealCourtCancelledCorrectFirstInstance = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_cancel definition appealMustBeCancelled equals No
```

## Article 353. Grounds for sending case for continued or new review

```catala
declaration scope Article353CassationSendForReview:
  input check content CassationSendForNewReviewCheck
  output mustSendForNewReview content YesNo
  output mandatoryCancellationApplies content YesNo
  output caseSentToAppealCourt content YesNo

scope Article353CassationSendForReview:
# Send for new review when procedural violation prevented establishing facts
  label evidence_not_examined definition mustSendForNewReview under condition
    check.sendForReviewGround = CassationSendForReviewGround.CourtDidNotExamineEvidence
    consequence equals Yes

  label simplified_instead_general definition mustSendForNewReview under condition
    check.sendForReviewGround = CassationSendForReviewGround.SimplifiedInsteadOfGeneral
    consequence equals Yes

  label rejected_motion definition mustSendForNewReview under condition
    check.sendForReviewGround = CassationSendForReviewGround.UnreasonablyRejectedEvidenceMotion
    consequence equals Yes

  label inadmissible_evidence definition mustSendForNewReview under condition
    check.sendForReviewGround = CassationSendForReviewGround.EstablishedFactsOnInadmissibleEvidence
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_send definition mustSendForNewReview equals No

# Mandatory cancellation for specific procedural violations
  label unauthorized_composition definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryCancellation = CassationMandatoryCancellation.UnauthorizedCourtComposition
    consequence equals Yes

  label recused_judge definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryCancellation = CassationMandatoryCancellation.RecusedJudgeParticipated
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_notified definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryCancellation = CassationMandatoryCancellation.ParticipantNotProperlyNotified
    consequence equals Yes

  label non_participant definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryCancellation = CassationMandatoryCancellation.RightsOfNonParticipantAffected
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_signed definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryCancellation = CassationMandatoryCancellation.DecisionNotSigned
    consequence equals Yes

  label wrong_judges definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryCancellation = CassationMandatoryCancellation.DecisionByWrongJudges
    consequence equals Yes

  label jurisdiction definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryCancellation = CassationMandatoryCancellation.JurisdictionViolation
    and check.participantRaisedJurisdictionInFirstInstance = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label jurisdiction_excused definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryCancellation = CassationMandatoryCancellation.JurisdictionViolation
    and check.participantRaisedJurisdictionInFirstInstance = No
    consequence equals No

  label not_mandatory definition mandatoryCancellationApplies equals No

# Case sent to appeal court when only they made violations
  label to_appeal definition caseSentToAppealCourt under condition
    check.violationOnlyByAppealCourt = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label to_first definition caseSentToAppealCourt equals No
```

## Article 354. Grounds for cancellation with closure or leave without consideration

```catala
declaration scope Article354CassationCloseOrLeave:
  input check content CassationCloseOrLeaveCheck
  output mustCancelAndCloseOrLeave content YesNo
  output administrativeJurisdictionViolationMandatory content YesNo
  output deathOrTerminationNotGround content YesNo

scope Article354CassationCloseOrLeave:
# Cancel and close or leave on grounds of Arts 238, 240
  label cancel_close definition mustCancelAndCloseOrLeave under condition
    check.closureGroundUnderArt238 = Yes
    or check.closureGroundUnderArt240 = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_cancel definition mustCancelAndCloseOrLeave equals No

# Administrative jurisdiction violation is mandatory ground
  label mandatory definition administrativeJurisdictionViolationMandatory under condition
    check.administrativeJurisdictionViolation = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_mandatory definition administrativeJurisdictionViolationMandatory equals No

# Death or termination after lawful decision is not ground
  label not_ground definition deathOrTerminationNotGround under condition
    check.deathOrTerminationAfterDecision = Yes
    and check.legalSuccessionNotPossible = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label may_be_ground definition deathOrTerminationNotGround equals No
```

## Article 355. Cassation court decisions and procedure

```catala
declaration scope Article355CassationDecisionsForm:
  input check content CassationDecisionsFormCheck
  output decisionsInFormOfPostanova content YesNo
  output proceduralQuestionsByRulings content YesNo
  output decisionsFinalAndNotAppealable content YesNo

scope Article355CassationDecisionsForm:
# Cassation court decisions in form of postanova
  label postanova definition decisionsInFormOfPostanova equals Yes

# Procedural questions resolved by rulings
  label rulings definition proceduralQuestionsByRulings equals Yes

# Cassation decisions are final and not appealable
  label final definition decisionsFinalAndNotAppealable equals Yes
```

## Article 356. Content of cassation court postanova

```catala
declaration scope Article356CassationPostanovaContent:
  output mustContainIntroductoryPart content YesNo
  output mustContainDescriptivePart content YesNo
  output mustContainMotivationalPart content YesNo
  output mustContainOperativePart content YesNo

scope Article356CassationPostanovaContent:
# Postanova must contain all four parts
  label introductory definition mustContainIntroductoryPart equals Yes

  label descriptive definition mustContainDescriptivePart equals Yes

  label motivational definition mustContainMotivationalPart equals Yes

  label operative definition mustContainOperativePart equals Yes
```

## Article 357. Late cassation complaint

```catala
declaration scope Article357CassationLateComplaint:
  input check content CassationLateComplaintCheck
  output lateComplaintConsidered content YesNo
  output mayStayPreviousDecisions content YesNo
  output refusalForAlreadyConsideredGrounds content YesNo

scope Article357CassationLateComplaint:
# Late complaint considered when arrived after review and complainant not present
  label considered definition lateComplaintConsidered under condition
    check.complaintArrivedAfterReviewEnded = Yes
    and check.complainantNotPresentAtReview = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_considered definition lateComplaintConsidered equals No

# May stay previous postanova and lower court decisions
  label may_stay definition mayStayPreviousDecisions under condition
    check.complaintArrivedAfterReviewEnded = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_stay definition mayStayPreviousDecisions equals No

# Refuse when grounds already considered
  label refuse definition refusalForAlreadyConsideredGrounds under condition
    check.groundsNotPreviouslyConsidered = No
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_refuse definition refusalForAlreadyConsideredGrounds under condition
    check.groundsNotPreviouslyConsidered = Yes
    consequence equals No
```

## Article 358. Separate ruling by cassation court

```catala
declaration scope Article358CassationSeparateRuling:
  output mayIssueSeparateRuling content YesNo

scope Article358CassationSeparateRuling:
# Cassation court may issue separate ruling per Art 249 rules
  label separate_ruling definition mayIssueSeparateRuling equals Yes
```

## Article 359. Entry into force of cassation court decisions

```catala
declaration scope Article359CassationEntryIntoForce:
  input check content CassationEntryIntoForceCheck
  output postanovaEntersIntoForceOnAdoption content YesNo
  output rulingEntersIntoForceOnPronouncement content YesNo
  output rulingOutsideSessionEntersOnSignature content YesNo

scope Article359CassationEntryIntoForce:
# Postanova enters into force on adoption
  label postanova_adoption definition postanovaEntersIntoForceOnAdoption under condition
    check.isResolution = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

# Ruling enters into force on pronouncement
  label ruling_pronouncement definition rulingEntersIntoForceOnPronouncement under condition
    check.isRuling = Yes
    and check.pronouncedInSession = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

# Ruling outside session or all absent or written enters on signature
  label ruling_signature definition rulingOutsideSessionEntersOnSignature under condition
    check.isRuling = Yes
    and (check.allParticipantsAbsent = Yes
    or check.isWrittenProceeding = Yes)
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_postanova definition postanovaEntersIntoForceOnAdoption equals No

  label not_ruling definition rulingEntersIntoForceOnPronouncement equals No

  label not_outside definition rulingOutsideSessionEntersOnSignature equals No
```

## Article 360. Return of administrative case

```catala
declaration scope Article360CassationCaseReturn:
  input check content CassationCaseReturnCheck
  output caseReturnedToFifteenDays content YesNo

scope Article360CassationCaseReturn:
# Case returned to first instance within 15 days after cassation review
  label fifteen_days definition caseReturnedToFifteenDays under condition
    check.daysSinceReviewEnded <= 15
    and check.differentDestinationSpecified = No
    consequence equals Yes

  label different_destination definition caseReturnedToFifteenDays equals No
```
